1
00:00:00,794 --> 00:00:03,494
(Penny:)- You're kidding.
- No, Raj had to go to the nurse.

2
00:00:03,664 --> 00:00:06,194
(Penny:)Wow. Anything else?

3
00:00:06,367 --> 00:00:10,237
(Leonard:)Mm, the nurse is a woman,
so he couldn't talk to her.

4
00:00:11,005 --> 00:00:14,705
She had to bring him the Grover puppet
so he could point at what hurt. Heh.

5
00:00:18,545 --> 00:00:20,275
(Penny:)Is that it?

6
00:00:20,447 --> 00:00:22,417
(Leonard:)Isn't that enough?

7
00:00:22,583 --> 00:00:26,213
It had weaponized fruit and a puppet.
What more do you want?

8
00:00:26,887 --> 00:00:28,377
(Sheldon(arriving with Alex):)Oh, good. Leonard, you're here.

9
00:00:28,555 --> 00:00:30,855
(Sheldon(arriving with Alex):)Science news. This will interest you.

10
00:00:31,025 --> 00:00:33,685
(Sheldon(arriving with Alex):)And, Penny,
feel free to paint your nails.

11
00:00:35,362 --> 00:00:37,952
- What do you got?
- I believe Alex may have unearthed...

12
00:00:38,132 --> 00:00:42,192
...the grade-school science project that
could be my ticket to the Nobel Prize.

13
00:00:42,369 --> 00:00:43,799
(Sheldon:)Behold.

14
00:00:43,971 --> 00:00:46,201
"Magnets: What Do They Stick To?"

15
00:00:48,342 --> 00:00:52,072
If the answer is metal,
it's not exactly groundbreaking.

16
00:00:52,246 --> 00:00:53,376
The original title was:

17
00:00:53,547 --> 00:00:57,247
"A Rederivation of Maxwell's Equations
Regarding Electromagnetism."

18
00:00:57,418 --> 00:01:00,748
(Sheldon:)I dumbed it down because some
of the more religious people in town...

